@prefix aegis: <http://aegis.gastown.local/ontology/> .
@prefix sh:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Directive deadline cardinality (aegis-b9k, sattler ruling 2026-11-28). A
# Directive has at most ONE traceability deadline, across the stable and the
# legacy predicate, and it is a typed, timezone-bearing xsd:dateTime. Camayoc's
# directive_deadline reader fails closed on two values; one such Directive
# stalled the whole directive-untraced adapter batch (ten were found and
# cleaned). Episode writes only add triples, so the graph must refuse the second
# value. REJECT (no quipu:onViolation annotation = default reject).
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT REFUSE (measured 2026-11-28 on quipu 0.19.5,
# scratch, both validate_on_write settings; aegis-b9k). Quipu validates the
# INCOMING write, not the stored state of its focus node. So this refuses a
# single write that carries two deadlines, or an untyped or zone-less one. It
# does NOT refuse a second deadline added by a LATER write (accepted through
# /knot and /episode alike), and with validate_on_write = false no stored shape
# gates /episode at all. The writer guard (graph-extract reads the graph first,
# aegis #769) and the quipu merged-state cardinality fix carry that case.
#
# STANDALONE on purpose. It says nothing about whether a Directive is traced or
# dated: an untraced, undated Directive stays a Warning in the pinned
# aegis-ontology DirectiveTraceabilityShape, because capture records a
# Directive verbatim first and links it afterwards.

aegis:DirectiveDeadlineCardinalityShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass aegis:Directive ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path [ sh:alternativePath ( <https://w3id.org/intigraph/quechua/ns#traceabilityDueAt> <https://scbrown.github.io/quechua/ns#traceabilityDueAt> ) ] ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:dateTime ;
        sh:pattern "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$" ;
    ] ;
    sh:message "A Directive has at most one traceabilityDueAt, a typed timezone-bearing xsd:dateTime (aegis-b9k)" .
